  "kind": "pose",
  "note": "Feeding: hunched over a catch held under the face. The head pitches nose-down over the meal, the abdomen lifts so the whole body arches, the front pair of legs draws in and up to hold it, and the chelicerae work it: the fangs pump in and out and open and close every other key while the body rocks over them once per four. Spine and head pitch are POSITIVE, which is nose-down; the thorax itself pitches only a little because every hip hangs off it and a real nose-down there lifts the back legs off the ground. The other six feet are pulled in toward the body so the lowered body has slack to reach the floor. Two rocks per loop, and the last key repeats the first so the clip cycles. The front feet are `unweighted` because they are holding food at rest height, not standing on it.",
